cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite the papers below."
title: "Heilbronn discovery lab: papers, certificates and verification code"
abstract: "Papers on the Heilbronn triangle problem in the unit square and the triangle, with data and code: computer-assisted optimality proofs for nine points in the square, eight points in a triangle and nine points in a triangle (the last with a replayable certificate trace), certificates for best-known square configurations for n = 37-100, and a study of critical triangles. The code was written with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hendren
    given-names: Ethan
license: [MIT, CC-BY-4.0]
date-released: 2026-11-18
keywords: [Heilbronn triangle problem, discrete geometry, computer-assisted proof, certificate trace, exact arithmetic]
